  "id": "mesial-temporal-lobe-epilepsy",
  "term": "mesial temporal lobe epilepsy",
  "definition": "Mesial temporal lobe epilepsy is a form of epilepsy that affects the inner part of the temporal lobe and is described here as the most common type seen in adults in surgical series. In this syndrome, hippocampal sclerosis has been used as a clinical sign linked to poor response to drug treatment.",
